Why Is Demand Increasing
Automotive Lightweighting: PPA resin provides high thermal stability, chemical resistance, mechanical strength, and lower weight, making it increasingly attractive for automotive and EV components.
Electronics Miniaturization: Strong dielectric properties, dimensional stability, and heat resistance support PPA use in miniature connectors, semiconductor packaging, and high-frequency electronic components.
Infrastructure and Industrial Applications: Expanding infrastructure and industrial activity, particularly across Asia-Pacific, is increasing demand for durable and chemically resistant engineering polymers.

PPA Resin Watch: High-Temperature Materials for EVs and Electronics
PPA resin is gaining strategic importance as manufacturers replace metals and conventional plastics with high-performance engineering polymers. Flame-retardant grades, advanced formulations, bio-based feedstocks, and additive manufacturing are broadening the material's application potential across automotive, electronics, medical, construction, and industrial markets.

